Replaced the linear scan with a one-time-built 16-bit index table that preserves first-match semantics by filling in reverse order. This makes `GetMesg` O(1) per call, which is especially faster for the full-domain sweep.

```cpp
const Profile::MESG* Profile::GetMesg(const FIT_UINT16 num)
{
    static FIT_UINT16 lookup[65536];
    static bool initialized = false;
    if (!initialized)
    {
        for (int i = MESGS - 1; i >= 0; --i)
            lookup[mesgs[i].num] = static_cast<FIT_UINT16>(i + 1);
        initialized = true;
    }

    const FIT_UINT16 idx = lookup[num];
    return idx ? &mesgs[idx - 1] : NULL;
}
```